  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "Fluid Simulation is the computational modelling of liquid and gas dynamics using numerical methods \u2014 notably computational fluid dynamics (CFD) and Navier-Stokes solvers \u2014 to produce physically plausible representations of water, smoke, fire, and atmospheric phenomena in real-time or offline rendering pipelines. In spatial computing and metaverse environments it contributes to environmental immersion and interactive physics, running on GPU compute shaders for performance-critical applications.",
